INT. ELIAB'S HOUSE - NIGHT #14#

The room is full: music and dancing, bread stacked high, the fires roaring, dust shaking up from the stamping feet. Asher sits at the table in the robe. His bread lies untouched. Under the table the dog lies across his feet and will not move.

ASHER
Let me earn it, Father. Put me with the hired men.

ELIAB
You are my son. Eat.

Asher turns to Micah.

ASHER
When does the flock go out?

MICAH
At first light, as it always has.

ASHER
Then I will be at the fold.

Micah looks at him, and nods.

MICAH
Your ewe is there. Your brother has kept her fat.

Asher looks at the door. Amos is not in the room.

